  "body": "#6714 clarified when a form submission should do a replace load. Step 23 in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#form-submission-algorithm now says:\r\n\r\n> If form document has not yet [completely loaded](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-lifecycle.html#completely-loaded), then set historyHandling to \"[replace](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#hh-replace)\".\r\n\r\nwith `form document` defined as\r\n\r\n> Let form document be form's [node document](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document).\r\n\r\nThat's pretty weird because it doesn't consider the `targetNavigable`, which can have an active document that's not `form document`. If `targetNavigable`'s active document has completely loaded we'll still do a replace load.\r\n\r\nI think it would make more sense to replace `form document` with `targetNavigable's active document`. From my limited testing that also looks to be closer to what Chrome implements.\r\n\r\n/cc @domenic @zcorpan @smaug---- ",
